edia.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fddd19139-52ef-4ee4-b0a6-efcb3e05bd90_884x588.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p><strong>Groovy 6 shipped structured concurrency as a Java library.</strong> Not a Groovy feature you can call from Java if you squint. A separate jar, <code>groovy-concurrent-java</code>, no Groovy runtime on the classpath, and this is the sample straight out of <a href=\"https://groovy-lang.org/releasenotes/groovy-6.0.html\">the release notes</a>:</p><pre><code>import groovy.concurrent.AsyncScope;\nimport org.apache.groovy.runtime.async.AsyncSupport;\n\nvar result = AsyncScope.withScope(scope -&gt; {\n    var a = scope.async(() -&gt; fetchUser(id));\n    var b = scope.async(() -&gt; fetchOrders(id));\n    return Map.of(\n        \"user\",   AsyncSupport.await(a),\n        \"orders\", AsyncSupport.await(b)\n    );\n});</code></pre><p>That is <code>StructuredTaskScope</code> with the serial numbers filed off. Which arrives in JDK 27 as <a href=\"https://openjdk.org/jeps/533\">JEP 533</a>, seventh preview, after two incubator rounds before that. Nine releases of refinement. Groovy needed one.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mNlC!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce292bef-b8dc-4add-8317-8f51cde22503_1120x816.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mNlC!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce292bef-b8dc-4add-8317-8f51cde22503_1120x816.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mNlC!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce292bef-b8dc-4add-8317-8f51cde22503_1120x816.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mNlC!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce292bef-b8dc-4add-8317-8f51cde22503_1120x816.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mNlC!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce292bef-b8dc-4add-8317-8f51cde22503_1120x816.png 1456w\" size