0 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><h3>tda, a Swing app from 2016 that grew an MCP server</h3><p><a href=\"https://github.com/irockel/tda\">TDA</a> by <strong>Ingo Rockel</strong> is the Thread Dump Analyzer, a Swing desktop tool that reads Java thread dumps and heap information, and supports Java 1.4.x through 21+, which tells you how long it has been doing it. In 3.0, back in January, it grew a <strong>Model Context Protocol server</strong>, with 3.1 and 3.2 following in April and May.</p><p>You start it with <code>java -Djava.awt.headless=true -jar tda.jar --mcp</code> and it exposes analysis as tools rather than handing a model a wall of stack traces. <code>analyze_virtual_threads</code> finds virtual threads whose carrier is stuck in application code. <code>get_zombie_threads</code> returns threads with unresolved SMR addresses. That is the pinning problem from this issue's PS, answered by something that already knows what pinning looks like, rather than by a model pattern-matching on text.</p><p>The operational notes are the part I enjoyed most. MCP speaks JSON-RPC over stdin and stdout, so the documentation warns that anything else printing to stdout corrupts the stream and drops the client. And a Swing application has to be told to skip its own UI initialisation before it can serve at all, which is a sentence nobody expected to write about a desktop tool.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!EE6_!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad1d6313-699f-4583-b003-a6d06db831b3_2560x940.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!EE6_!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad1d6313-699f-4583-b003-a6d06db831b3_2560x940.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!EE6_!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad1d6313-699f-4583-b003-a6d06db831b3_2560x940.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!EE6_!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad1d6313-699f-4583-b003-a6d06db831b3_2560x940.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!EE6_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad1d6313-699f-4583-b003-a6d06db831b3_2560x940.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!EE